>Faux_Pseudo wrote:
>> And what is the best way to kill a priest?
>
>I'd say, explore elsewhere, tame a pony/horse/warhorse, and train it up
>to maximum level.  They can take out priests, although it might be
>close.  But this way, you keep the blood off your hands.
>
>If that's too much trouble, try killing it with wands or spells from
>outside the temple, as if you fight inside you'll also have lightning
>bolts from the temple's deity to worry about.
>

  Rocks have been recommended for kills from outside the temple.
As well as digging out one side so the priest can be hit no
matter where he is in the temple.

  Scroll/spell of charm monster may be of help.  If the priest
doesn't resist and if you can avoid getting killed trying it.
I believe a ring of free action is necessary to keep the priest
from paralyzing you at close range.  Confused scroll of taming
might help there.

  Ring of conflict combined with powerful monsters in the temple
may help.

  I'd say avoid the priest for now unless it's urgent to kill 
him.  Maybe even dig down if the downstairs are in the temple.
(Be prepared to not come up until you've got surefire means
of handling the priest, i.e. mollifying or killing.)
Dig a path around the temple if it's a choke point between
up and down stairs.

  Hope for scroll of taming or spell of charm monster.
Maybe magic harp/flute.  I think flute puts monsters to sleep,
and harp tames.  Check before you try.

  You're big problem is getting back in good with your god.
Giant mimics are supposed to be good for this.  Don't think
unicorns will help.  Check the spoilers.  

  I've been in that situation as a chaotic Wizard with spell of 
create monster.  It took a long time, and a surprising number of 
monsters I considered powerful were sacrificed without helping 
the divine anger situation.

  If you haven't got much divine protection consider doing the 
quest then converting to another alignment.  Then killing the
priest yourself won't cause as much trouble.

  Use this advice at your own risk.  Check facts using spoilers,
etc.

